   "reply": "I put your floor plan into mojulo as a house, with all seven rooms at the sizes on your drawing, and designed the three rooms you asked to see. You can open them at these links:\n\n- **House:** `/sketches/sk_8c79eurf5c`\n- **Lounge:** `/sketches/sk_v52u713phl`\n- **Dining room:** `/sketches/sk_am3heosp4v`\n- **Big bedroom:** `/sketches/sk_zkbkm9d498`\n\nI haven't opened any of the renders, so I haven't checked how the rooms look.\n\nI placed the doors and windows with mojulo's defaults, so they may not match your drawing exactly. The house link is the one to check.\n\n- **Lounge (modern-organic with wabi-sabi touches):** The sofa faces the wide north windows. Two armchairs and a rug make a conversation group around a coffee table. A reading nook with a lamp sits in the far corner, and two bookcases line the south wall. I left out a TV, so the room is built for talking and reading.\n- **Dining room (modern-farmhouse with warm-minimal touches):** There's a farmhouse table with six Windsor chairs on a big rug, and a sideboard and a bookcase for storage. It only has one overhead light, so I'd add a pendant over the table and a lamp on the sideboard.\n- **Big bedroom (warm-minimal with japandi touches):** A king bed has a nightstand on each side, with a rug under it. There's a dresser on the west wall and a reading chair with a lamp by the windows. The mojulo bed tops out at 2000 mm, so it's slightly narrower than a standard king. The reading chair also didn't get a side table, because there wasn't room.\n\nI can change the styles, move pieces, or try a different scheme for any room, such as a fireplace in the lounge or wood-paneled walls in the bedroom."
